<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=zipper">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zipper</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Zip fastener, Clasp locker</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A zipper is a device for binding together two edges of fabric or other flexible material, with a slider that meshes or separates two rows of interlocking teeth. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elias-howe">Elias Howe</a> received a patent in 1851 for an improvement in fastenings for garments, more like a drawstring than a true slide fastener. In 1893 Whitcomb L. Judson patented a shoe fastening, his clasp locker, shown at the Chicago World's Fair. Gideon Sundbäck, a Swedish-American engineer, redesigned it and the zipper first went on sale in 1913; his Separable Fastener patent was issued in 1917. The name comes from a brand of galoshes in 1923.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zipper.jpg" alt="Zipper" width="330" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Woodbine9 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coil_plastic_and_metal_zippers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1893</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Chicago, United States</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Whitcomb L. Judson · Gideon Sundbäck · <a href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Elias Howe patented an 'Improvement in Fastenings for Garments' in 1851, but it was more like an elaborate drawstring than a slide fastener. Judson's device was not used in clothing.</p><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=zipper">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
